{"created": "2026-03-22T18:44:28.105085+00:00", "modified": "2026-03-22T18:45:19.095045+00:00", "id": 19164291, "conceptrecid": "19164290", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19164291", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.19164290", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19164291", "metadata": {"title": "Fine-tuned Faster-R-CNN for detection and classification of blue and fin whale calls in low-frequency audio data", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19164291", "publication_date": "2026-03-22", "description": "<p>This repository contains the weights for a fine-tuned Faster R-CNN object detection model trained to detect blue and fin whale calls in 60-second spectrograms from passive acoustic recordings. The model detects five call types: blue whale A, B, and D calls, and fin whale 20 Hz and 40 Hz calls.</p>\n<p>The model uses a ResNet-50 backbone with a feature pyramid network and was fine-tuned from a pretrained checkpoint over three rounds of human-in-the-loop refinement on high-frequency acoustic recording package (HARP) and California Cooperative Oceanic Fisheries Investigation (CalCOFI) sonobuoy recordings from the Southern California Current Ecosystem. The final training dataset comprised 11,676 annotated calls across both recording platforms. The model operates on 60-second spectrograms computed with a 1-s Hamming window and 90% overlap, band-limited to 10&ndash;150 Hz. Audio is partitioned into non-overlapping 60-second clips, spectrograms are normalized individually between 0&ndash;1, and mapped to an 8-bit integer tensor.</p>\n<p>Code for running inference or retraining the model is available at <a href=\"https://github.com/m1alksne/WhaleMoanDetector\">https://github.com/m1alksne/WhaleMoanDetector</a>.</p>", "access_right": "restricted", "creators": [{"name": "Alksne, Michaela Noel", "affiliation": "University of California San Diego", "orcid": "0009-0002-2284-1639"}, {"name": "Roch, Marie A.", "affiliation": "San Diego State University"}, {"name": "Frasier, Kaitlin", "affiliation": "Scripps Institution of Oceanography", "orcid": "0000-0002-2401-8569"}, {"name": "Hildebrand, John", "affiliation": "Scripps Institution of Oceanography", "orcid": "0000-0002-5418-9799"}, {"name": "Andres, Shane", "affiliation": "University of California San Diego"}, {"name": "Adesanya, Dolapo", "affiliation": "University of California San Diego"}, {"name": "Baggett, Lauren", "affiliation": "University of California San Diego", "orcid": "0009-0008-2403-2513"}, {"name": "Jones, Joshua M.", "affiliation": "University of California San Diego"}, {"name": "Liu, Xiaobai", "affiliation": "San Diego State University"}, {"name": "\u0160irovi\u0107, Ana", "affiliation": "Norwegian University of Science and Technology"}, {"name": "Zhang, Xixin", "affiliation": "San Diego State University"}, {"name": "Zingale, Joshua", "affiliation": "San Diego State University"}, {"name": "Baumann-Pickering, Simone", "affiliation": "University of California San Diego", "orcid": "0000-0002-3428-3577"}], "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/m1alksne/WhaleMoanDetector", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}], "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "active", "title": {"en": "Active"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Model", "type": "model"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "19164290"}}]}}, "title": "Fine-tuned Faster-R-CNN for detection and classification of blue and fin whale calls in low-frequency audio data", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19164291", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19164291", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19164291?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19164291", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19164291", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.19164291", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19164291/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.